# NADEEN DESIGNS – PROJECT CONSTITUTION v1.0

These rules override implementation convenience.

## Mission

Build a luxury bridal ecommerce platform — scalable, maintainable, and fully manageable from the Admin Panel. Not just a website.

## Rule #1 — No hardcoded business data

Never hardcode: categories, products, collections, homepage sections, payment methods, shipping methods, store information, social links, contact information, SEO, or business texts.

Everything comes from the database.

## Rule #2 — Admin-manageable by default

Anything the business owner may want to change in the future belongs in the Admin Panel. Never require code edits for business operations.

## Rule #3 — Module quality

Every new module must be: Dynamic, Reusable, Scalable, Production Ready.

## Rule #4 — Admin First

The business owner should manage the store without touching code.

## Rule #5 — Customer Experience first

Never sacrifice UX for implementation simplicity.

## Rule #6 — Definition of done

Every module must pass: Manual QA, TypeScript, ESLint, Production Build, Responsive, RTL, Accessibility, No Console Errors.

## Rule #7 — Root cause only

Do not create temporary fixes. Always solve the root cause.

## Rule #8 — Design for growth

Every feature must support future growth: 5,000+ products, 300+ categories, thousands of customers.

## Rule #9 — Module independence

Modules must remain independent. Avoid tight coupling.

## Rule #10 — Luxury UX

Minimal. Elegant. Fast. Clean.

## Current development order

1. Store Settings
2. Navigation
3. Product Management
4. Checkout
5. Orders
6. Homepage Builder
7. Analytics

No unrelated work before completing the current module.
